cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Human transcutaneous spinal cord stimulation — EMG analysis
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a study of arm muscle EMG responses to
  transcutaneous spinal cord stimulation in healthy volunteers. Two
  stimulation protocols — 30 Hz monophasic bursts and ARC-EX (a 10 kHz
  carrier at the same pulse rate) — are compared under topical lidocaine,
  tendon vibration, stimulation polarity and pulse rate. Includes
  hand-picked per-muscle motor thresholds, per-pulse peak-to-peak response
  amplitudes and response latencies for four participants.
